Fix B1 in a *copy* of the Bazaar fixture (E:\bazaar stays read-only).

The defect: `CartStore.add()` never sets `qty` on the entry it inserts, then
increments the *previous* entry's quantity. The second add of the same product
unboxes a null `Integer` and throws
`java.lang.NullPointerException: Integer.intValue`.

Apply from the fixture root with `git apply -p1 demo/CartStore.java.diff`, or let
`demo/build_fixed_apk.ps1` do the copy+patch+build.

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/bazaar/demo/CartStore.java b/app/src/main/java/com/bazaar/demo/CartStore.java
index 70f42d6..f7abbf5 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/bazaar/demo/CartStore.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/bazaar/demo/CartStore.java
@@ -31,17 +31,18 @@ public final class CartStore {
 
     public static void add(Product p) {
         Entry existing = findById(p.id);
 
         Entry e = new Entry();
         e.product = p;
-        // qty is intentionally left null here; syncWithServer() was meant to set it.
+        e.qty = 1; // every new cart entry starts at one
         ITEMS.add(e);
 
         if (existing != null) {
-            existing.qty = existing.qty + 1; // B1: NullPointerException on 2nd add
+            int previous = existing.qty == null ? 0 : existing.qty;
+            existing.qty = previous + 1; // null-safe: fixed B1
         }
     }
 
     private static Entry findById(String id) {
         for (Entry e : ITEMS) {
